---
import Base from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
import ChooseTool from "@/components/ChooseTool";
---

<Base
  title="Help me choose a car"
  description="Answer three questions about budget, body type and priorities - we rank every car in our database using EPA data, NHTSA records and a transparent cost model."
>
  <ChooseTool client:load />
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4">
    <section class="mt-12 border-t border-slate-200 pt-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">How the car chooser works</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-ink-soft">
        The tool first removes vehicles outside your budget and requested body type. It then
        compares the remaining cars using the priorities you select. Every candidate uses the
        same mileage, ownership period and energy-price assumptions, so a lower cost or higher
        ranking comes from the vehicle data rather than a hidden weighting or sponsored result.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-5">
          <p class="text-sm font-bold text-brand-dark">1. Set the limits</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-ink-soft">
            Choose a purchase budget and the body style that fits your daily use.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-5">
          <p class="text-sm font-bold text-brand-dark">2. Pick priorities</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-ink-soft">
            Balance total cost, efficiency, cargo, performance, safety signals and price.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-5">
          <p class="text-sm font-bold text-brand-dark">3. Verify the trade-off</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-ink-soft">
            Open the top pair to inspect every specification and cost assumption side by side.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Useful starting points</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-ink-soft">
        Not sure which filters to choose? Start with one of these researched buyer situations,
        then change the comparison to match your own budget and driving.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-5 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <a href="/best/best-family-suv-under-40k" class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-5 transition hover:border-brand">
          <h3 class="font-semibold">Family SUV under $40k</h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-6 text-ink-soft">Compare space, safety and five-year cost.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/best/best-commuter-car" class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-5 transition hover:border-brand">
          <h3 class="font-semibold">High-mileage commuter</h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-6 text-ink-soft">See when fuel savings offset the purchase price.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/best/best-first-car" class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-5 transition hover:border-brand">
          <h3 class="font-semibold">First car under $30k</h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-6 text-ink-soft">Prioritize affordability, efficiency and safety.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/methodology" class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-5 transition hover:border-brand">
          <h3 class="font-semibold">Review our methodology</h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-6 text-ink-soft">Understand every source, estimate and limitation.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
